{"shortDescription":"China’s global exports of electric vehicles rose 33% Y/Y in August to 284,622 units, bringing year-to-date total exports to 2.11M vehicles (+53% Y/Y), according to Bloomberg reporting citing China Customs data.As per the report, Belgium retained its position as the single largest country importer o…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["China’s global exports of electric vehicles rose 33% Y/Y in August to 284,622 units, bringing year-to-date total exports to 2.11M vehicles (+53% Y/Y), according to Bloomberg reporting citing China Customs data."]},{"type":"p","children":["As per the report, Belgium retained its position as the single largest country importer of Chinese EVs during the month, with shipments surging 76% Y/Y to 32,538 units (213,001 units YTD)."]},{"type":"p","children":["Australia followed as the second-largest destination with 22,067 units (+106% Y/Y), while Brazil recorded significant growth, jumping 353% Y/Y to 20,154 units. Rounding out the top five destinations were Thailand with 17,718 units (+66% Y/Y) and the United Kingdom with 17,297 units (+18% Y/Y)."]},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"seekingalpha:5e96d8622094b-615b8fc37ca30ec33e7792c416ac24b9","alt":"Bloomberg","source-width":791,"source-height":637,"bg-color":"#efefef"}}},{"type":"p","children":["By region, Asia remained China's largest market by volume in August, importing 108,757 units (+2.5% Y/Y), followed by Europe with 94,912 units (+33% Y/Y). Within Europe, shipments specifically destined for the European Union increased 31% Y/Y to 63,825 units. Meanwhile, Latin America and the Caribbean experienced strong growth among major markets, surging 118% Y/Y to 43,742 units, while Oceania saw shipments rise 121% Y/Y to 25,201 units, the report said."]},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"seekingalpha:5e96d8622094b-8f432f96664460261e68c630d3b67b79","alt":"Bloomberg","source-width":786,"source-height":558,"bg-color":"#eeeeee"}}},{"type":"p","children":["The surge in international shipments reflects how Chinese automakers are increasingly leveraging overseas markets across Europe, Asia, and Latin America to drive volume and offset competitive domestic pressures."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Related auto players in China:"]}," Nio (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:NIO","text":"NYSE:NIO"}},"), XPeng Inc (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:XPEV","text":"NYSE:XPEV"}},"), Li Auto (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:LI","text":"NASDAQ:LI"}},"), BYD (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:BYDDY","text":"OTC:BYDDY"}},") and Tesla (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:TSLA","text":"NASDAQ:TSLA"}},"), Great Wall Motor (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:GWLLF","text":"OTC:GWLLF"}},"), (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:GWLLY","text":"OTC:GWLLY"}},"), Geely Automobile (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:GELYF","text":"OTC:GELYF"}},"), Toyota (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:TM","text":"NYSE:TM"}},"), Volkswagen (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:VLKAF","text":"OTC:VLKAF"}},"), Guangzhou Automobile Group (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:GNZUF","text":"OTC:GNZUF"}},"), Wuling Motors (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:WLMTF","text":"OTC:WLMTF"}},"), Nissan (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:NSANY","text":"OTC:NSANY"}},"), BAIC (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:BCCMY","text":"OTC:BCCMY"}},"), Zotye, state-owned SAIC Motor, Beiqi Foton, Chery and Dongfeng Motor (",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/DNFGY?utm_source=tradingview\u0026utm_medium=referral\u0026feed_item_type=news","linkText":"DNFGY"}},").",{"type":"disclaimer","children":["Content provided by Seeking Alpha is intended for information purposes only, and that Seeking Alpha does not offer any personalist investment advice and is not a licensed securities dealer